# Sedge Beast — a Two-color Lesser enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 4/12 Two-color Lesser enemies — 16 life, bribe 70 gold
# enemy: Sedge Beast (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0219.dck "Sedge Beast (R/B, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink
#   3 file dated 2016-02-15; its first 13 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 14 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/sedge_beast.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 4)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/sedge_beast.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Lesser) — "Sedge Beast" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Sedge Beast
10 Mountain
10 Swamp
4 Strip Mine
2 Dancing Scimitar
4 Uthden Troll
4 Stone Rain
4 Blight
4 Fissure
4 Erg Raiders
4 Ironclaw Orcs
4 Cyclopean Mummy
2 Diabolic Machine
2 Immolation
2 Weakness
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   2 Weakness, 1 Immolation
#   .vBlack  2 Hurr Jackal, 1 Immolation
#   .vBlue   2 Weakness, 1 Immolation
#   .vGreen  2 Weakness, 1 Immolation
#   .vRed    2 Weakness, 1 Immolation
#   .vWhite  2 Weakness, 1 Immolation
SB: 2 Hurr Jackal
